        truths: ("{DL} radioed patrol officers to 'skip that block' the same week.", "Old holiday cards show the owner and {DL} swapped gifts for years."),
        defendant: [.direct("Was it a bribe?", "\"No. It was a birthday gift from an old friend. I accepted it at a parking lot and said thank you.\""), .direct("Why the cash?", "\"The owner always gave cash. Every year, an envelope with a few bills in it, and a small gift.\""), .direct("Why meet in a parking lot?", "\"It was easiest. I was on duty nearby and stopped for a minute.\""), .direct("What did you mean by 'understood'?", "\"I meant thank you. The owner said something about keeping the block quiet, and I said understood as a way to be polite.\""), .direct("Did you skip checks at the bar?", "\"I did not order anyone to skip. Patrol assignments rotate, and I do not set every check.\""), .direct("What do you want the court to know?", "\"I never sold my badge. I took a gift from a friend, and I should have thought about how it looked.\""), .cross("$500 and ballgame tickets is a large gift, isn't it?", "\"It is generous. It is what the owner always gave.\""), .cross("The owner says it bought quiet nights, doesn't the owner?", "\"The owner says so now, to help the owner's case.\""), .cross("No checks were logged at that bar for six weeks, were they?", "\"I did not control that. I did not tell anyone to skip the bar.\""), .cross("You said 'understood' when told it was for keeping the block quiet, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I took it as small talk.\""), .cross("You accepted it from a bar owner in a parking lot while in uniform, didn't you?", "\"Yes. That looks bad, I know.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, a police sergeant, accepted $500 and a pair of ballgame tickets from a bar owner who wanted police to skip after-hours checks. An SBI wire recorded the owner saying 'for keeping the block quiet' and {D} answering 'understood.'", "The tickets and money were a birthday gift from an old friend who gave gifts every year. A sergeant who says thank you is not selling quiet nights."),
        closings: ("A wire recording, cash and tickets, six weeks with no after-hours checks, and a sergeant who said 'understood.' A gift tied to quiet nights is a bribe.", "An old friend, a yearly gift, and a word that meant thank you. The State must prove {D} agreed to skip the checks."),
