        defense: [E(.forensic, 2, "Lab Contamination", "Two analysts handled the glove and the lab log has gaps."), E(.forensic, 2, "Unknown Fingerprint", "A fingerprint on the back door belongs to no one tested."), E(.document, 1, "Alibi App", "A sleep app on {DL}'s phone shows rest overnight.")],
        role: "Homicide detective",
        exam: [.direct("Walk the jury through your work as a homicide detective.", "\"I investigate killings. I examine scenes, review DNA and camera evidence, and interview witnesses and suspects.\""), .direct("What happened at about 3 a.m. on {DATE}?", "\"Four university students, {V} and three roommates, were stabbed to death in a second-floor apartment near campus.\""), .direct("What did the fifth roommate hear and see?", "\"The fifth roommate, asleep in a back room, heard the front lock click and saw a figure in a gray hooded sweatshirt leave.\""), .direct("What did you find in the stairwell?", "\"A latex glove in the trash. Skin cells inside the glove matched {D}'s profile in a state database.\""), .direct("What did the garage camera show?", "\"A hatchback with a partial plate similar to {D.his} leaving at 3:15 a.m.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the sweatshirt?", "\"{D.He} bought a gray hooded sweatshirt two weeks earlier. A receipt shows it.\""), .cross("Who else's print was found?", "\"A fingerprint on the back door belonged to no one tested at first. Later it matched a delivery driver with a protective order from one of the victims.\""), .cross("Was there a boot print?", "\"Yes. A boot print in the stairwell matched boots in {DL}'s trunk, with a victim's blood in the tread.\""), .cross("Is {D} from this area?", "\"No. {D.He} is a graduate student in another city. {D.He} says {D.he} was home asleep, and a sleep app shows rest overnight.\""), .cross("Was the glove handled by more than one analyst?", "\"Yes. Two analysts handled the glove, and the lab log has gaps. That raises a question about contamination.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant at the apartment?", "\"No. No one saw {D.him}. We have the glove, the hatchback, and the sweatshirt, and no eyewitness.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Independent DNA analyst",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do as an independent DNA analyst?", "\"I review DNA evidence for the defense and the prosecution. I examine lab logs, chain of custody, and contamination risks.\""), .direct("What did you review in this case?", "\"The glove, the lab log, and the profile. I looked for how the glove was handled and whether the log is complete.\""), .direct("What did you find about the lab log?", "\"Two analysts handled the glove, and the log has gaps. Gaps make it hard to rule out contamination.\""), .direct("What does a match to a state database profile mean?", "\"It means the profile matches a person in the database. It does not say when or how the cells got on the glove.\""), .direct("Could touch DNA be transferred to a glove?", "\"Yes. Skin cells can transfer by contact with other items. It is rare, but it is possible, especially if handling was loose.\""), .direct("What would you want to see before relying on this match?", "\"A complete log, separate handling, and testing of other items. I did not see those in this case.\""), .cross("Does the glove match {D}'s profile?", "\"Yes. The profile matches. I did not dispute the match, only the handling.\""), .cross("Did you find evidence of contamination?", "\"No. I found gaps that make it impossible to rule out contamination. I cannot say contamination occurred.\""), .cross("Did you examine the stairwell?", "\"No. I only reviewed the lab work. I cannot say how the glove got there.\""), .cross("Could the cells have been left in the killing?", "\"Yes. They could have been. I cannot rule that out, and I do not claim to.\""), .cross("Is touch DNA transfer common?", "\"It is not common. It happens, but I cannot say it happened here.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} killed four students and left a glove behind.", "A tainted sample and no firm tie to the scene."),
        allocution: "\"I have nothing to say that will bring them back.\"",
        truths: ("A boot print in the stairwell matched boots in {DL}'s trunk, with a victim's blood in the tread.", "A partial print on the back door matched a delivery driver who had a protective order from one of the victims."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please tell us about your life as a graduate student.", "\"I study in another city. I work long hours in a lab, and I do not know the people who lived in that apartment.\""), .direct("Where were you at 3 a.m. that night?", "\"Home asleep. A sleep app on my phone shows rest overnight. I did not travel to that city.\""), .direct("Why does a glove carry your DNA?", "\"I do not know. It could have been tampered with. My profile is in a state database, and I did not leave it there.\""), .direct("Why did you buy a gray sweatshirt?", "\"I bought it for the cold. Many people have the same sweatshirt, and I wore it often.\""), .direct("What about the hatchback?", "\"I own a hatchback, like thousands of others. It did not leave a garage in that city that night.\""), .direct("How do you feel about being accused?", "\"If I am honest, I feel terrified. Four people died, and I am accused. I did not do it, and I want the real killer found.\""), .cross("The glove matches your profile, doesn't it?", "\"So the lab reports. I do not know how my skin cells got there.\""), .cross("You bought a gray hooded sweatshirt two weeks earlier, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. It is a common sweatshirt, and I wore it at home.\""), .cross("A hatchback like yours was on the camera, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. But it is a common car. I was not in it.\""), .cross("A boot print matched boots in your trunk, didn't it?", "\"I am told so. I do not know how a victim's blood could be in the tread. I was not there.\""), .cross("No one can confirm you were asleep, can they?", "\"No. I was alone. The sleep app shows rest, and I know that is not proof.\"")],
        openings: ("At about 3 a.m. on {DATE}, four university students, {V} and three roommates, were stabbed to death in a second-floor apartment near campus. A latex glove in the stairwell trash carried DNA matching {D}, and a hatchback like {D}'s left a parking garage at 3:15 a.m.", "The defense will present a sleep app showing rest overnight, a lab log with gaps, a fingerprint on the back door that belongs to someone else, and an independent DNA analyst. The State must prove it was {D}."),
        closings: ("A glove with {D}'s DNA in the stairwell, a hatchback on the garage camera, a gray sweatshirt bought two weeks earlier, and a boot print with a victim's blood in the tread. The evidence points to {D}.", "A lab log with gaps, a fingerprint that belongs to a delivery driver with a protective order, and a person asleep in another city. The State has not proved that {D} was in the apartment."),
        timeline: [(-14, "{DL} buys a gray hooded sweatshirt."), (0, "About 3:00-3:20 a.m.: four students killed; a hatchback leaves the garage."), (0, "Morning: the roommate calls 911."), (30, "The glove profile matches {DL}."), (35, "{DL} is arrested.")],
        identified: "DNA on a latex glove found in the stairwell trash.",
        aggravating: ["The offense involved multiple victims", "The offense was especially heinous, atrocious, or cruel"],
        mitigating: ["No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "expertTestimony"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let deadWomanAccountsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.deadWomanAccounts",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Man Opened Credit Cards in Dead Woman's Name to Buy Truck", "Dealership Video Shows Buyer After Obituary Ran"],
        law: "identityTheft",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Knowingly obtained and used identifying information of {V}, a deceased person, to obtain credit, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Three weeks after {V} died, new credit applications in {V.his} name led to a $48,000 truck loan at a dealership on {DATE}. The dealership's video shows {D} signing. {DL} says {V} had given {D.him} written authority to handle {V.his} affairs.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Credit Applications", "Three applications use {V}'s Social Security number and {D}'s phone."), E(.video, 3, "Dealership Video", "{D} signs the loan papers at the finance desk."), E(.document, 2, "Death Certificate", "{V} died twenty-two days before the loan.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Written Authority", "{DL} says {V} signed a power of attorney.")],
        role: "Auto finance manager",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your work as an auto finance manager.", "\"I process loan applications at a dealership. I verify identity, review credit, and prepare the papers that buyers sign.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"Three weeks after {V} died, new credit applications in {V}'s name led to a $48,000 truck loan at our dealership.\""), .direct("What did the credit applications show?", "\"Three applications used {V}'s Social Security number and {D}'s phone number. That connected {DL} to the applications.\""), .direct("What does the dealership video show?", "\"It shows {DL} signing the loan papers at the finance desk. {DL} signed as if {DL} were {V}'s representative.\""), .direct("How long had {V} been dead?", "\"Twenty-two days before the loan. The death certificate shows the date.\""), .direct("What did you learn about {D}'s searches?", "\"{DL} asked an online forum how to keep a dead person's credit active. That drew my attention.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say {V} gave authority?", "\"Yes. {DL} said {V} signed a power of attorney. A signed form was found in {V}'s safe deposit box, dated four months before death.\""), .cross("Is a power of attorney valid after death?", "\"No. It ends at death. But {D.he} may not have known that, and I cannot say what {D.he} understood.\""), .cross("Did the defendant show the form at the dealership?", "\"I do not recall. The file does not include the form. I processed the loan on the applications.\""), .cross("Did the defendant sign {V}'s name?", "\"{DL} signed as a representative. I do not know whether the signature was misleading.\""), .cross("Did you check whether {V} had died?", "\"No. We did not. The applications looked ordinary, and the death was not in our checks.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Notary",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What does your work as a notary involve?", "\"I notarize documents and verify identities. I keep a journal of every signature and the date I witnessed it.\""), .direct("What do you remember about the power of attorney?", "\"I notarized it four months before {V} died. {V} came in, signed, and showed identification. It was a real signature.\""), .direct("How did {V} seem when signing?", "\"Clear and sure. {V} told me {V} wanted {D} to handle affairs, and I noted that in my journal.\""), .direct("Where was the form kept?", "\"In {V}'s safe deposit box. It was found after death. It was properly signed and dated.\""), .direct("What does a power of attorney cover?", "\"It lets the agent act for the person while the person is alive. It ends at death, and many people do not know that.\""), .direct("Did {D} ask you anything about it?", "\"Once, after the death. {D.He} asked if it was still valid. I said I was not sure, and I told {D.him} to ask a lawyer.\""), .cross("Does a power of attorney continue after death?", "\"No. It ends. I told {D.him} to check, and I do not know whether {D.he} did.\""), .cross("Did you notarize anything for the loan?", "\"No. I only notarized the power of attorney. I had nothing to do with the loan.\""), .cross("Did the defendant tell you {V} had died?", "\"Yes. After the death. I said I was sorry. I did not know the loan was being taken.\""), .cross("Could the defendant have known the authority ended?", "\"Possibly. I mentioned I was not sure. I cannot say what {D.he} knew when signing.\""), .cross("Did {V} sign anything about credit?", "\"Not with me. I only notarized the power of attorney. I do not know about any other forms.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used a dead person's identity to buy a truck.", "A power of attorney signed while {V} was alive."),
        allocution: "\"I am ashamed of what I did with that name.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} asked an online forum how to keep a dead person's credit active.", "A signed power of attorney form was found in {V}'s safe deposit box, dated four months before death."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please describe your relationship with {V}.", "\"{V} was a family friend. {V} trusted me to handle affairs, and gave me a power of attorney four months before death.\""), .direct("Why did you sign the loan papers?", "\"I believed the power of attorney covered it. I thought I was handling {V}'s affairs as {V} wanted.\""), .direct("Did you know the authority ended at death?", "\"No. I did not. I thought it still applied. I learned later that it does not.\""), .direct("Why did you ask an online forum about credit?", "\"I was trying to understand how to handle {V}'s accounts after death. I did not mean to hide the death.\""), .direct("Where did the loan money go?", "\"For a truck. I used it as I thought {V} would have wanted, and I know that does not make it right.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"I would say I feel terrible. I made a serious mistake. I did not mean to defraud anyone, and I truly am sorry.\""), .cross("{V} had been dead twenty-two days, hadn't {V}?", "\"Yes. I know. I did not tell the dealership. I wish I had.\""), .cross("You used {V}'s Social Security number on three applications, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I believed I had authority, and I know it was wrong.\""), .cross("You asked how to keep a dead person's credit active, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I asked. I was confused and I was not thinking clearly.\""), .cross("You did not tell the dealership {V} had died, did you?", "\"No. I did not. I know how that looks, and I should have told them.\""), .cross("The power of attorney was signed four months before death, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I know it ended at death. I did not know that then.\"")],
        openings: ("Three weeks after {V} died, new credit applications in {V}'s name led to a $48,000 truck loan at a dealership on {DATE}. The applications used {V}'s Social Security number and {D}'s phone, and the dealership video shows {D} signing.", "The defense will present a written power of attorney signed four months before death, a notary who saw {V} sign it, and a person who believed it still applied. A mistake about the law is not a fraud."),
        closings: ("Three applications with {V}'s Social Security number, {D}'s phone number, a signature on video, and a death twenty-two days earlier. {D} also asked a forum how to keep a dead person's credit active.", "A power of attorney signed and notarized four months before death, and a person who believed it covered the loan. The State has not proved that {D} meant to commit fraud."),
        timeline: [(-120, "The power of attorney is notarized."), (-22, "{V} dies."), (0, "Truck loan signed at the dealership."), (30, "The finance company flags the death record.")],
        identified: "Dealership video and credit applications.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let parkingOfficeSafeV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.parkingOfficeSafe",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Parking Authority Cash Drawers Emptied After Overnight Break-In", "Palm Print on Window Latch Leads to Former Contractor"],
        law: "feloniousBE",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Broke and entered a building of {V}, a parking authority, with intent to commit larceny therein, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, a rear window of a parking authority office was pried open and $9,100 in meter and kiosk cash was taken from desk drawers. A palm print on the window latch matched {D}, and a license plate reader recorded {D}'s car nearby. {DL} says {D.he} once worked in the office and left a print then.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Palm Print", "A palm print on the window latch matches {D}."), E(.digital, 3, "Plate Reader Hit", "{D}'s car passes the lot at 2:10 a.m."), E(.document, 2, "Cash Count", "$9,100 missing from the drawers.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Past Work", "{DL} says {D.he} fixed the window months earlier.")],
        role: "Authority director",
        exam: [.direct("How would you describe your job as an authority director?", "\"I run the parking authority. I manage staff, meters, kiosks, and the cash that we collect and deposit.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"A rear window of our office was pried open and $9,100 in meter and kiosk cash was taken from desk drawers.\""), .direct("What did the police find?", "\"A palm print on the window latch that matches {D}. A license plate reader recorded {D.his} car nearby at 2:10 a.m.\""), .direct("How much was taken?", "\"$9,100. We counted the drawers afterward, and the missing cash matches the day's collections.\""), .direct("What did you learn about {D}'s past work?", "\"{D.He} once worked in the office and fixed the window months earlier. That could explain a print, and I considered it.\""), .direct("What was found in the defendant's garage?", "\"A pry bar with window paint chips. It matches the marks on our window frame.\""), .cross("Where was the palm print on the latch?", "\"On the inside of the latch. Work orders show a cleaning a week earlier, so the print could be recent.\""), .cross("Did the defendant have a key to the building?", "\"Not now. {D.He} left months ago. I do not know whether {D.he} kept a key.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant at the office?", "\"No. No one saw {D.him}. We have the print and the plate reader, and no eyewitness.\""), .cross("Could a print remain on a latch after months?", "\"Yes, in theory. But the cleaning a week earlier makes me doubt it.\""), .cross("Did the defendant cooperate with investigators?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said {D.he} once worked here and left a print then. {D.He} did not argue.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Former coworker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Tell the jury how you know {D}.", "\"I worked with {D} at the parking authority. We shared an office for years, and I know {D.him} as honest and hardworking.\""), .direct("What did the defendant do about the window?", "\"{DF} fixed the latch months earlier. I saw {DF} working on it, and {DF} used a tool kit from the office.\""), .direct("How often was the window cleaned?", "\"Not often. But work orders show a cleaning a week before the break-in. I do not know who did it.\""), .direct("Did the defendant ever take anything from the office?", "\"Never. {DF} handled small cash at times and always turned it in. I never had a reason to doubt {DF}.\""), .direct("What did you think when you heard about the defendant?", "\"I was shocked. I could not believe it. I told the investigators that {D.he} would not do something like this.\""), .direct("Who else had access to the window?", "\"Several current and former employees. A cleaner also had access. I cannot say who touched the latch.\""), .cross("Did the defendant still have a key?", "\"I do not know. I did not see {DF} return one. I cannot say whether {DF} kept it.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} near the office that night?", "\"No. I was not there. I only know what the records say.\""), .cross("Was the defendant having money trouble?", "\"I do not know. I did not discuss it with {D.him}.\""), .cross("Could the defendant's print be from the earlier repair?", "\"Possibly. But the cleaning makes it less likely. I cannot say for certain.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever mention the cash drawers?", "\"Not that I recall. {DF} knew where they were, as we all did, but never mentioned them.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} pried a window and emptied the drawers.", "A print left during repair work."),
        allocution: "\"I did something stupid.\"",
        truths: ("A pry bar with window paint chips was in {DL}'s garage.", "{DL}'s palm print was on the inside of the latch, where work orders show a cleaning a week earlier."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please tell us about your time at the parking authority.", "\"I worked in the office for several years. I fixed small things, including the window latch, and I knew the building well.\""), .direct("How did your palm print get on the latch?", "\"I fixed the window months earlier. I left a print then, and I did not think it could last.\""), .direct("Where were you at 2:10 a.m.?", "\"Driving home. The plate reader shows my car near the lot. I live nearby and I often drive that way.\""), .direct("Did you break into the office?", "\"No. I did not. I would never steal from a place where I worked.\""), .direct("What about the pry bar in your garage?", "\"I use it for projects. It has paint chips from my own work, and I do not know whether they match the window.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"I am hurt. I worked there for years, and now I am accused of stealing from my old employer.\""), .cross("Your palm print is on the latch, isn't it?", "\"Yes. It is. I know how it looks, but I left it when I fixed the window.\""), .cross("A cleaning was done a week earlier, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. The work order says so. I do not know how my print stayed, but it did.\""), .cross("Your car was near the lot at 2:10 a.m., wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I was driving home. I know the time is late, and I know that looks suspicious.\""), .cross("A pry bar with paint chips was in your garage, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It is an ordinary tool. I use it for many things.\""), .cross("$9,100 is a lot of cash, isn't it?", "\"Yes. I have never seen that much cash in that office. I did not take it.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, a rear window of a parking authority office was pried open and $9,100 in meter and kiosk cash was taken from desk drawers. A palm print on the window latch matched {D}, a plate reader recorded {D}'s car nearby, and a pry bar was in {D}'s garage.", "The defense will present a former employee who fixed that window and left a print long before, a pry bar used for ordinary projects, and a drive home. A print left earlier is not a break-in."),
        closings: ("A palm print on the latch, a plate reader hit at 2:10 a.m., a pry bar with window paint chips in {D}'s garage, and $9,100 gone. The print was on the inside of the latch after a cleaning.", "A former coworker who fixed the window and left a print then, and a drive home on a familiar road. The State has not proved that {D} broke into the office."),
        timeline: [(-90, "{DL} repairs the window latch."), (0, "2:10 a.m.: {DL}'s car passes the lot."), (0, "7 a.m.: staff find the window open."), (3, "The print matches {DL}.")],
        identified: "A palm print and a plate reader.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction)

    static let ticketTearScreamV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.ticketTearScream",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Driver Screams at Tow Operator and Kicks Truck While Car Is Hooked", "Dash Camera Shows Kick and Shouting"],
        law: "disorderly",
        spec: "Disturbed the peace by violent conduct at a street tow, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "At 3:20 p.m. on {DATE}, a tow operator hooked {D}'s car for parking in a posted tow zone. {D} ran from a nearby shop, screamed at the operator and kicked the tow truck's door. A crowd gathered. The operator called deputies and {D} refused to leave until they arrived at 3:40 p.m. {D} says {D.he} was only upset about the cost.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Tow Truck Dash Camera", "{D} screams at the operator and kicks the door at 3:22 p.m."), E(.statement, 2, "Tow Operator", "Was hooking the car in a posted tow zone."), E(.document, 2, "Posted Sign", "A tow zone sign above the space."), E(.document, 2, "Deputy's Report", "Found {D} still shouting at 3:40 p.m.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Upset About Cost", "{DL} says {D.he} was upset about the cost."), E(.document, 1, "Tow Rate Sheet", "A posted rate sheet showing a $210 tow fee.")],
        role: "Tow operator",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your work as a tow operator.", "\"I hook cars that are parked in posted tow zones. I follow the signs and the rules, and I try to be fair with drivers.\""), .direct("What happened at 3:20 p.m. on {DATE}?", "\"I hooked {D}'s car for parking in a posted tow zone. A sign above the space says it is a tow zone.\""), .direct("What did {D} do?", "\"{D.He} ran from a nearby shop, screamed at me, and kicked my truck's door. The dash camera caught it at 3:22.\""), .direct("What happened next?", "\"A crowd gathered. I called deputies, and {DL} refused to leave until they arrived at 3:40.\""), .direct("What was the tow fee?", "\"$210, as listed on the posted rate sheet. That is the standard fee in that zone.\""), .direct("How did the defendant behave while waiting?", "\"{DL} kept shouting and was still shouting when the deputy arrived. {DL} did not calm down until the deputy spoke.\""), .cross("Had the defendant been towed from that space before?", "\"Yes. {D.He} had been towed from the same space twice. I did not know that at the time.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say anything about the sign?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said {D.he} had not seen the sign and was upset about the fee.\""), .cross("Did the defendant hit you?", "\"No. {D.He} kicked the door of the truck. {D.He} did not touch me, and I was not hurt.\""), .cross("Was the crowd a danger?", "\"No. People gathered to watch. I felt uncomfortable, but I was not threatened.\""), .cross("Was {D} cooperative with the deputy?", "\"Yes. Once the deputy arrived, {DL} calmed down and left. {DL} apologized.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Shop clerk",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Describe your work as a shop clerk.", "\"I work at the shop next to the tow zone. I see cars parked and towed there often, and I know many of the people who use the space.\""), .direct("What did you see that afternoon?", "\"I saw {D} run out and shout at the tow operator. {D.He} looked upset and desperate.\""), .direct("How was the sign positioned?", "\"It is above the space, high on a pole. Many drivers do not see it from where they stand.\""), .direct("What do you know about {D}'s finances?", "\"{D.He} has had a hard time. A $210 fee is a big deal. I could see why {D.he} was so upset.\""), .direct("How did the defendant behave afterward?", "\"{DF} calmed down when the deputy arrived. {DF} said sorry and left. I have never seen {DF} act like that before.\""), .direct("What kind of person is the defendant?", "\"Polite and hardworking. {D.He} loses patience rarely. That afternoon was an exception.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant kick the truck?", "\"Yes. I saw it. I was surprised, and I did not try to stop {D.him}.\""), .cross("Did the defendant threaten the operator?", "\"I heard shouting. I did not hear a specific threat, but I was not close.\""), .cross("Did you see the sign?", "\"Yes. It is there. But many drivers miss it, and I understand how that could happen.\""), .cross("Did {D} refuse to leave?", "\"Yes. {DF} stayed until the deputy arrived. I think {DF} wanted the car back.\""), .cross("Has the defendant been towed before?", "\"I heard so. I do not know how often. {D.He} has parked there at times.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} screamed and kicked a tow truck.", "{D} was upset about the tow fee."),
        allocution: "\"I understand why people were afraid. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been towed from the same space twice.", "{DL} had not seen the sign and was upset about the fee."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please describe your shop and the space.", "\"I work at the shop nearby, and I park in that space when I can. I have been towed from there twice before.\""), .direct("Why did you run to the truck?", "\"I saw my car being towed. I was upset about the cost and I ran out to ask the operator to stop.\""), .direct("Did you see the sign?", "\"No. I did not see it. I thought the space was fine, and I am upset about the sign.\""), .direct("Why did you scream?", "\"I was angry about another $210. I have struggled with money, and I could not afford another fee.\""), .direct("Why did you kick the truck door?", "\"I lost my temper. I did not mean to damage anything. It was a reaction, and I know it was wrong.\""), .direct("Why did you stay until the deputy arrived?", "\"I wanted my car back. I was still upset, and I did not want to leave without it. I apologized after.\""), .cross("You kicked the truck's door, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I regret it, and I know it was wrong.\""), .cross("You screamed at the operator, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was loud. I did not threaten anyone, but I was out of control.\""), .cross("You had been towed from that space twice before, hadn't you?", "\"Yes. I know I should have learned. I did not notice the sign.\""), .cross("A tow zone sign was posted above the space, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I did not look up. I know it was there.\""), .cross("You refused to leave until deputies arrived, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I wanted my car. I know I should have left, and I apologize.\"")],
        openings: ("At 3:20 p.m. on {DATE}, a tow operator hooked {D}'s car for parking in a posted tow zone. {D} ran from a nearby shop, screamed at the operator and kicked the tow truck's door, then refused to leave until deputies arrived at 3:40.", "The defense will present a person who did not see the sign, who was upset about a $210 fee, and who apologized to the deputy. An outburst over a tow is not a crime of intent."),
        closings: ("A tow truck dash camera that shows {D} screaming and kicking the door, a posted sign above the space, a crowd gathering, and a refusal to leave until deputies arrived. {D} had been towed there twice before.", "A person who had never seen the sign and who was desperate over a $210 fee. The State has not proved that {D} meant to disrupt anything beyond an upset about cost."),
