        role: "State Highway Patrol trooper",
        exam: [.direct("How would you describe your job as a State Highway Patrol trooper?", "\"I investigate crashes on state and county roads. I examine the scene, check the vehicle, and review phone and vehicle records.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"A car crossed onto a grass median at 55 miles an hour and knocked over a road sign. {D} was driving.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you?", "\"{D.He} said a tire blew. I checked the tires, and I found a tire in good condition.\""), .direct("What did the crash report show?", "\"No braking marks. The car left the road without any attempt to slow down, which is unusual for a tire failure.\""), .direct("What did the phone log show?", "\"A video call active until two seconds before the crash. That is a very short time before the car left the road.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the screen-time log?", "\"It shows {DL} was scrolling a social app in the minute before the crash. That is on the phone, not on the car.\""), .cross("Could the call have been hands-free?", "\"{D.He} says so, and the car's infotainment log shows a voice-only call routed through the speaker. I cannot say that the video call was also running.\""), .cross("Was the defendant looking at the phone when the car left the road?", "\"I cannot say. The log shows scrolling in the minute before. It does not show what {D.he} was looking at at the moment of the crash.\""), .cross("Did the defendant cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D.He} gave a statement and showed the phone. {D.He} said the call ran through the car's speaker.\""), .cross("Was anyone hurt?", "\"No. There were no injuries beyond a bruise. The sign was knocked over, and the car was damaged.\""), .cross("Could a tire failure leave no braking marks?", "\"It could, if the driver lost control quickly. But the tire was in good condition, so I doubt it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} was on a video call and left the road.", "A driver on a hands-free call."),
        allocution: "\"I was not paying attention. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("A screen-time log shows {DL} was scrolling a social app in the minute before the crash.", "The car's infotainment log shows a voice-only call routed through the speaker."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about your drive that day.", "\"I was driving home on the highway. I was on a call, and I was talking through the car's speaker.\""), .direct("Why did you tell the trooper a tire blew?", "\"It felt like something went wrong with the car. I did not know what happened, and I said the first thing that came to mind.\""), .direct("Were you using your phone in your hand?", "\"No. I was using the car's hands-free system. The call ran through the speaker, and the screen was on a mount.\""), .direct("What about the scrolling log?", "\"I may have glanced at the screen. I did not scroll while driving, and I do not know why the log shows it.\""), .direct("What do you remember about the crash?", "\"A bump and a loud sound. I was looking ahead and then the car was on the grass. I do not remember steering.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about what happened?", "\"I feel lucky no one was hurt. I should have paid more attention, and I will keep my phone away while driving.\""), .cross("A video call was active until two seconds before the crash, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was. But I was using the speaker. I did not look at the screen.\""), .cross("You told the trooper a tire blew, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I was confused and I said that. It was not true.\""), .cross("There were no braking marks, were there?", "\"No. I did not brake. I do not know why. I was startled.\""), .cross("You were scrolling a social app in the minute before, weren't you?", "\"The log says so. I may have glanced at it. I do not remember scrolling.\""), .cross("The tire was in good condition, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I know. I was wrong about the tire.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, a car crossed onto a grass median at 55 miles an hour and knocked over a road sign. {D} told the trooper that a tire blew, but a video call was active until two seconds before the crash, and the tire was in good condition.", "The defense will present a hands-free system that carried the call through the car's speaker, and a driver who was startled and said the wrong thing. A call on a speaker is not texting in hand."),
