        openings: ("On {DATE}, a diner filmed {D}, a server, swiping a card through a small reader below the tableside terminal and then through the register. Nine diners reported fraud within days, a reader was found in {D}'s car, and {D} used one of the copied cards to buy a game console.", "The defense will present a reader that the manager bought, instructions to use it when the terminal was slow, and servers who all had access. {D} did not copy cards on purpose."),
        closings: ("A video of a card swiped twice, nine compromised cards, a reader in {D}'s car, and a game console bought with a copied card. The evidence points to {D}.", "A backup reader ordered by the manager and kept in an open office, and a server who used it as told. The State has not proved that {D} meant to copy cards."),
        timeline: [(-10, "The first fraud alerts."), (0, "7 p.m.: the double swipe on video."), (2, "The diner shares the clip."), (3, "The car is searched.")],
