        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Oven Wiring", "{DL} says an oven wire sparked.")],
        role: "Fire investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What does your work as a fire investigator involve?", "\"I determine how fires start. I examine burn patterns, collect samples, and send them to the lab for accelerants.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"A fire began in the back alley of a bakery just after 2 a.m. and climbed into the apartment above, where {V} slept and escaped through a window.\""), .direct("What did you find at the alley wall?", "\"Gasoline residue. The lab confirmed it. That suggests the fire was set, not an electrical accident.\""), .direct("What did the gas station video show?", "\"{D}, the bakery's owner, buying a fuel can and filling it at 1 a.m.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the bakery's finances?", "\"It owed $70,000 and had a foreclosure notice. The overdue notices were in the file.\""), .direct("What was in the dumpster?", "\"A gasoline-soaked rag with {D.his} apron. I bagged it and sent it to the lab.\""), .cross("Could an oven wire have started the fire?", "\"{D.He} says so. A manufacturer recall notice for the oven's wiring was in the shop mail, dated a month before the fire.\""), .cross("Was the fire in the oven area?", "\"No. It began in the back alley, outside the building. An oven wire would not start a fire in the alley.\""), .cross("Did {D} say why {D} bought the fuel can?", "\"{D.He} said it was for a generator. I did not find a generator at the bakery.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant start the fire?", "\"No. No one saw it. My conclusion is from the residue, the video, and the rag.\""), .cross("Was {V} hurt?", "\"{V} escaped through a window and was not seriously injured. I was glad, and I know it could have been worse.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Electrician",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What are your duties as an electrician?", "\"I install and repair electrical systems. I have worked on commercial ovens and know how they fail.\""), .direct("What do you know about the oven's wiring?", "\"There was a manufacturer recall for the wiring. A faulty wire can spark, especially when a unit is old.\""), .direct("Can a spark start a fire outside the building?", "\"It can, if it ignites something near the wall. A fire in an alley can start from sparks or hot debris.\""), .direct("What did you see at the bakery?", "\"Old wiring and signs of heat. I told the investigators about the recall notice.\""), .direct("Why might the notice have been missed?", "\"It was in the shop mail. Small business owners often miss notices, especially when they are busy.\""), .direct("What do you think about the fire?", "\"It could have been electrical. I cannot say it was, but it is possible, and I would not rule it out.\""), .cross("Did you inspect the alley wall?", "\"No. I only inspected the oven. I cannot say what happened in the alley.\""), .cross("Did you find gasoline?", "\"No. I am not a fire investigator. I did not test for it.\""), .cross("Can an oven wire ignite gasoline?", "\"If gasoline was present, a spark could ignite it. But I do not know whether it was present.\""), .cross("Did {D} ask you to inspect the oven?", "\"Yes. After the fire. I told {D} what I found, and I gave a report.\""), .cross("Could the fire have been set?", "\"Possibly. I cannot rule it out. I only say the wiring could be another cause.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned the bakery's wall, endangering a tenant, to escape debt.", "A faulty oven cable."),
        allocution: "\"I never meant for anyone to be upstairs.\"",
        truths: ("A gasoline-soaked rag with {DL}'s apron was in the bakery dumpster.", "A manufacturer recall notice for the oven's wiring was in the shop mail, dated a month before the fire."),
        defendant: [.direct("What can you tell us about your bakery?", "\"I own a family bakery. I work long hours, and I pour everything into it. The business was struggling, but I loved it.\""), .direct("Did you set the fire?", "\"No. I did not. I would never burn my own bakery or put anyone at risk.\""), .direct("Why did you buy a fuel can at 1 a.m.?", "\"For a generator. We had a power problem, and I needed fuel. I filled the can and left.\""), .direct("What caused the fire?", "\"A faulty oven wire. A recall notice was in the shop mail a month before, and I did not read it.\""), .direct("Why was your apron in the dumpster with gasoline?", "\"I used a rag to clean the generator. The rag and apron were in the dumpster. I did not know it mattered.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"Terrible, more than anything. {V} could have died. I am glad {V} escaped, and I am sorry for the fire.\""), .cross("The bakery owed $70,000, didn't it?", "\"Yes. It was a hard time. I did not burn it for money.\""), .cross("You bought a fuel can at 1 a.m., didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I know the time looks bad, but I had a reason.\""), .cross("Gasoline was on the alley wall, wasn't it?", "\"That is what the investigator says, and I cannot explain the residue.\""), .cross("A foreclosure notice was in the file, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I knew. I did not want to lose the bakery, and I would not have burned it.\""), .cross("You never read the recall notice, did you?", "\"No. I did not. I wish I had read it before the fire.\"")],
        openings: ("A fire began in the back alley of a bakery just after 2 a.m. on {DATE} and climbed into the apartment above, where {V} slept and escaped through a window. Investigators found gasoline residue on the alley wall, and {D}, the bakery's owner, had bought a fuel can at 1 a.m.", "The defense will present a faulty oven wire that a manufacturer recalled, a notice that sat in the shop mail, and a fuel can bought for a generator. An accident is not an arson."),
        closings: ("Gasoline residue on the alley wall, a fuel can bought at 1 a.m., a $70,000 debt, a foreclosure notice, and a gasoline-soaked rag with {D}'s apron. {V} slept above the fire.", "A recalled oven wire, a notice that sat unopened, and a generator fuel can. The State has not proved that {D} set the fire."),
        timeline: [(-30, "A foreclosure notice reaches the bakery."), (0, "1 a.m.: the fuel can is bought."), (0, "2:10 a.m.: the fire starts in the alley."), (0, "2:20 a.m.: {V} escapes through a window.")],
        identified: "Gas station video and fire investigation.",
        aggravating: ["The offense endangered the lives of many people"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        genders: ["V": .female])

    static let mallBanReturnV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.mallBanReturn",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Shopper Banned From Big-Box Store Returns for Groceries", "Ban Notice Went Out by Certified Mail"],
        law: "trespass2",
        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a retail store, after being notified not to, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} was banned in writing from a big-box store after a shoplifting incident in May. On {DATE} a loss-prevention officer found {D} in the grocery aisle and called deputies. {DL} says the notice was sent to an old address and was never received.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Ban Notice", "A written ban for one year dated May 8."), E(.video, 2, "Store Camera", "{D} walks in at 6:15 p.m. and picks up a basket.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Old Address", "{DL} says the notice went to an address {D.he} left in April.")],
        role: "Store loss-prevention officer",
        exam: [.direct("Tell the jury what you do at the store and how a ban works.", "\"I'm a loss-prevention officer at a big-box store. When someone is caught shoplifting, a manager issues a written ban for a set period, and the ban is entered in our system.\""), .direct("What did the ban for {D} say, and when was it issued?", "\"It was a one-year ban dated May 8, after an incident involving unpaid merchandise. The notice says that returning to the store during the ban would be treated as trespass.\""), .direct("How was the notice delivered?", "\"By certified mail to the address on file, and a copy was taped inside the front door. The mail receipt shows it was sent on May 9.\""), .direct("What did you see on the day in question?", "\"At 6:15 p.m., {D} walked in, picked up a basket, and went to the grocery aisle. I recognized {D.him} from the ban photo and confirmed it in the system.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called the sheriff's office and watched until deputies arrived at about 6:30. I did not approach {DL} or ask {D.him} to leave before they came.\""), .direct("How did the defendant behave while in the store?", "\"Calmly. {D.He} shopped in the grocery aisle and did not do anything disruptive, and there was no confrontation.\""), .cross("Was the certified letter ever signed for?", "\"No. It came back unsigned and marked as returned, which tells me no one at that address accepted it.\""), .cross("Was the defendant told in person about the ban?", "\"Not that I know of. The ban was issued by mail and a notice at the door.\""), .cross("Did you personally see the defendant read the notice at the door?", "\"No. A clerk told me about it later, but I didn't see it myself.\""), .cross("Was the defendant shoplifting or causing a problem that day?", "\"No. {DL} had a basket and was shopping like any other customer.\""), .cross("Would you agree {D} could have honestly missed the notice?", "\"It's possible. I can only say the ban was issued and mailed.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} returned during a one-year ban.", "A notice never received."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I did not know.\"",
        truths: ("A clerk photographed {DL} reading the ban notice taped to the front door.", "The certified mail receipt shows the notice was returned from an old address."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell us about the day you were banned.", "\"I was caught with unpaid items in May. A manager took a photo, told me there'd be a notice, and I walked out without any paper in my hand.\""), .direct("Where were you living at the time?", "\"At an apartment I left in April, though I hadn't updated everything. I was moving between a friend's place and a new rental.\""), .direct("Did you receive anything from the store?", "\"No letter, no call, and nothing in my new mailbox. If a notice was mailed to the old address, I never saw it.\""), .direct("Why did you go to the store that evening?", "\"I needed groceries and it's the closest store to my place. I took a basket and went to the grocery aisle like I always do.\""), .direct("What happened when deputies came?", "\"They told me I'd been banned for a year. I said I had no idea and asked to see the notice.\""), .direct("What did you do after that?", "\"I left when they asked and haven't been back. I'd have stayed away if I'd known.\""), .cross("A notice was taped to the front door. Didn't you see it?", "\"I didn't read signs on the door. I walk in the way I always have.\""), .cross("You moved in April and the ban came in May. Didn't you tell the store your new address?", "\"No. I didn't think the store needed it.\""), .cross("You were caught with unpaid items. Didn't you expect a ban?", "\"I figured there'd be some consequence, but I didn't know it was a written one-year ban.\""), .cross("A clerk says you were seen reading the notice. Is that true?", "\"I don't recall that. I may have glanced at a sign without reading the words.\""), .cross("Why not call the store to ask?", "\"It didn't occur to me. I assumed it was over.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} was banned in writing from this store for one year after a shoplifting incident in May. On the day in question, {D} walked back in, picked up a basket, and shopped for fifteen minutes.", "{D} says the ban was mailed to an old address and never arrived. The defense will show a certified letter returned unsigned and a shopper who had no idea {D.he} was barred."),
        closings: ("A written ban dated May 8, a certified letter that went out on May 9, and {D} inside the store at 6:15 p.m. on the date in question. The store gave notice the way the law allows, and {D} returned anyway.", "The certified letter came back unsigned, no one told {D} in person, and {D} acted like any customer once inside. The State has to prove {D} knew about the ban, and the mail receipt shows only that it was returned."),
        timeline: [(-120, "The shoplifting incident."), (-100, "The ban notice is mailed."), (0, "6:15 p.m.: {DL} walks into the store."), (0, "6:30 p.m.: deputies arrive.")],
        identified: "Store loss-prevention officer.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["mistakeOfFact"])

    static let dirtBikeStreetV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.dirtBikeStreet",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Four-Wheeler Weaves Down County Road as Church Lets Out", "Parent's Phone Video Shows Stunts at 50 mph"],
        law: "recklessDriving",
        spec: "Drove a motor vehicle on a highway carelessly and heedlessly in willful disregard of the rights and safety of others, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...30,
        victim: false,
        summary: "On {DATE}, a deputy was told a four-wheeler was doing wheelies at about 50 mph down a county road as an evening church service let out, weaving around parked cars and walkers. A parent's phone video showed {D}, who has no license, on the machine. {DL} says the road was empty and {D.he} saw no one.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Parent's Phone Video", "{D} on two wheels at speed, weaving past cars and walkers."), E(.statement, 2, "Deputy", "The deputy saw the four-wheeler leave the road and speed away.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Empty Road", "{DL} says the road was empty.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("Tell the jury what call you responded to that evening.", "\"At about eight, dispatch said someone on a four-wheeler was doing wheelies on a county road as a church service was letting out. I headed that way.\""), .direct("What did you see when you arrived?", "\"I saw a four-wheeler leave the road and speed away through a field. I couldn't catch it, but I got there in time to see the machine and a rider in a dark jacket.\""), .direct("How did you identify the rider?", "\"A parent at the church had filmed the whole thing on a phone. The video shows the four-wheeler on its back wheels, weaving past parked cars and people on the shoulder.\""), .direct("How fast was it going?", "\"I estimated about fifty miles an hour from the video and from the distance covered. The road has a limit of thirty-five.\""), .direct("Who is on the video?", "\"{D}, who has no driver's license and was identified by the parent and later by a social media post.\""), .direct("Were there people on the road?", "\"Several. Families were walking to their cars along the shoulder, and a few cars were pulling out of the church lot.\""), .cross("Did the four-wheeler hit anyone or anything?", "\"No. It came close to a couple of parked cars, but no one was struck.\""), .cross("Did you see any person who had to jump out of the way?", "\"I saw people step back on the video. I can't say anyone was in danger of being hit.\""), .cross("Was the road open to vehicles at that hour?", "\"Yes. It's a county road with no closure.\""), .cross("How long was the video?", "\"About forty seconds. The riding is clear, but the parent's phone was far away.\""), .cross("Did {D} try to flee from you personally?", "\"I didn't speak to {D.him} that night. I only saw the machine speed away.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} did stunts at speed past a church crowd.", "A skilled rider on an empty road."),
        allocution: "\"I was showing off. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s social page bragged, 'tore up the church road tonight.'", "The pastor said the service ended an hour earlier and the lot was empty."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please describe your four-wheeler.", "\"It's an old machine I bought used. I ride it on county roads near my house, and I do some wheelies when the road is clear.\""), .direct("What were you doing that evening?", "\"Riding to see a friend. I took the county road past the church because it's straight and usually quiet.\""), .direct("Did you see people in the road?", "\"I didn't see anyone. The lot was empty when I went past, and the road looked clear.\""), .direct("How fast were you going?", "\"Fast, maybe forty. I wasn't looking at the speedometer, and I know it's more than the limit.\""), .direct("Why did you post about it?", "\"It was a joke. I wrote that I'd torn up the church road, and I regret it now.\""), .direct("What did you do when you saw a deputy?", "\"I left the road and took off through a field. I panicked, because I don't have a license.\""), .cross("You've said the road was empty. The video shows families and cars. How do you explain that?", "\"I didn't see them. I was concentrating on keeping the front wheel up, and I wasn't looking.\""), .cross("You bragged about it online. Doesn't that show you knew what you were doing?", "\"It shows I thought it was funny. I didn't think about who might be nearby.\""), .cross("You don't have a license. Why ride on a public road?", "\"It's a four-wheeler and I thought the rules were different. I was wrong.\""), .cross("The pastor says the service ended an hour earlier and the lot was empty. Is the pastor wrong?", "\"I don't know. I only know what I saw at the moment I went by.\""), .cross("You fled a deputy. Isn't that consciousness of guilt?", "\"It's fear. I knew I'd be in trouble for the license, and I ran.\"")],
        openings: ("A four-wheeler on its back wheels, weaving past parked cars and families leaving church at about fifty miles an hour. A parent filmed it, and a deputy saw the machine leave the road.", "Jurors will meet a young rider on a quiet county road who thought it was clear, never saw anyone in danger, and made a joke online that now looks worse than the riding was."),
        closings: ("The video shows the four-wheeler on two wheels, past a church letting out, at about fifty on a road posted at thirty-five. The rider had no license and ran from a deputy.", "No one was touched. The road was open to traffic, the video is brief, and the people in it may not have been as close as they look. A reckless ride is not the same as endangering a crowd on purpose."),
        timeline: [(0, "7:40 p.m.: the church service ends."), (0, "8 p.m.: the four-wheeler runs the road."), (0, "8:20 p.m.: a deputy gets the video.")],
        identified: "A parent's phone video.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let coastalBodiesV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.coastalBodies",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Moving Company Worker Charged in Canal Killings", "Blanket Fibers and Coffee Lid DNA Link Suspect to Three Women"],
        law: "murder1",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "With premeditation and deliberation, killed {V}, whose remains were found in a tidal canal off Highway 70.",
        ages: 50...62,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Twelve years ago, the bodies of three young women, each wrapped in a blue moving blanket, were found in a drainage canal off Highway 70 over two weeks. The case went cold. Last year a task force matched the blankets to a regional moving company and a cell tower dump to a phone near all three disposal sites. A coffee lid {D} threw away at a gas station carried DNA that matched a hair on the blanket around {V}. {DL}, a longtime mover with no record, says {D.he} never knew the women and that the hair sample is too degraded to trust.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Blanket Hair DNA", "A hair on the blanket around {V} matches DNA from {D}'s coffee lid."), E(.digital, 3, "Tower Dump", "A phone tied to {D} near all three disposal sites."), E(.document, 2, "Blanket Inventory", "The blankets match stock from the moving company where {D} worked."), E(.statement, 2, "Van Sighting", "A fisherman saw a white moving van near the canal.")],
        defense: [E(.forensic, 3, "Degraded Sample", "The hair sample was partial and old."), E(.document, 2, "Shared Blankets", "Moving companies sold used blankets in bulk."), E(.document, 1, "Tower Coverage", "The tower covers eight miles of roads.")],
        role: "Task force detective",
        exam: [.direct("Tell the jury about your role on the task force.", "\"I'm a detective assigned to a cold-case task force on three homicides from twelve years ago. We re-examined the physical evidence and the phone and vehicle records.\""), .direct("How were the bodies found?", "\"Over two weeks, in a drainage canal off Highway 70. Each victim was wrapped in a blue moving blanket, and the first was {V}.\""), .direct("What led you to the moving company?", "\"Lab analysis showed the blankets were a particular brand and weave. That brand was sold to a regional moving company, and the inventory matched the stock.\""), .direct("What did the cell tower data show?", "\"A phone tied to {D} connected to towers near all three disposal sites at about the times the bodies would have been left. We obtained the records through warrants.\""), .direct("How did you get DNA from {D}?", "\"An undercover officer collected a coffee lid {DL} threw away at a gas station. The lab compared it to a hair found on the blanket around {V}, and the profiles matched.\""), .direct("What else tied the defendant to the area?", "\"A fisherman reported a white moving van near the canal during the relevant weeks. {D.He} drove a company van of that description at the time.\""), .cross("How many people worked for that moving company?", "\"About forty movers over the years. I interviewed twelve, but not all.\""), .cross("Is the blanket brand unique to that company?", "\"No. It's a common brand, and moving companies sell used blankets in bulk.\""), .cross("How many phones connected to those towers during the relevant windows?", "\"Hundreds. The tower covers about eight miles of roads, and our data shows only that {D.his} phone was in that area.\""), .cross("How degraded was the hair sample?", "\"It was partial and old. The lab did a partial profile and was able to compare it, with limited confidence.\""), .cross("Did you recover any victim's property from the defendant's home or van?", "\"No. We found nothing from the victims in the places we searched.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Defense DNA analyst",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your field, and what did you review?", "\"I'm a DNA analyst. I reviewed the lab's reports and the raw data from the hair and the coffee lid.\""), .direct("How many markers were used in the comparison?", "\"Only a partial profile, fewer than the standard thirteen. The hair was old and had very little nuclear DNA to work with.\""), .direct("What does that mean for the reliability of the match?", "\"It increases the chance that someone else could match by coincidence. I'd say the statistics are weaker than the report suggests.\""), .direct("Can mitochondrial DNA tell you who left a hair?", "\"It can only narrow it to a maternal line, not an individual. A match would be shared by everyone related on the maternal side.\""), .direct("Could the hair have come from someone else?", "\"Yes. Without a better sample, I can't exclude other possible donors.\""), .direct("How should a jury treat a partial profile?", "\"With caution. It's evidence, but it should be weighed alongside the other facts.\""), .cross("Isn't it consistent with {D}?", "\"It can be. I'm not saying {D} is excluded, only that the sample is weak.\""), .cross("You didn't test the hair yourself, did you?", "\"No. I reviewed the lab's data and notes. I did not have the sample.\""), .cross("Did the coffee lid profile match the hair's profile at every marker tested?", "\"At the markers tested, yes. The issue is how few markers there were.\""), .cross("Have you testified for the defense before?", "\"Yes, many times. I'm paid for my time, not for my conclusions.\""), .cross("If more markers had been available, could the match be stronger?", "\"It could be, or it could exclude {DF}. I can't say which.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} wrapped three women in moving blankets and left them in a canal.", "A weak hair sample and a common blanket."),
        allocution: "\"I cannot say anything.\"",
        truths: ("A storage unit rented under an alias by {DL} held blankets and a bracelet that belonged to one of the victims.", "A second hair from another blanket excluded {DL} and matched a man already in prison for a similar killing."),
        defendant: [.direct("Describe your work for the jury.", "\"I've worked as a mover for twenty-two years. I drive company vans across the region and I've never been arrested.\""), .direct("Did you know {V} or the other victims?", "\"No. I'd never seen them before I read about the case. I don't know anything about how they died.\""), .direct("Why was your phone near the canal?", "\"My route runs along Highway 70. I drive it three or four times a week, and that area is on a lot of my deliveries.\""), .direct("Where did the blankets come from?", "\"They're standard equipment in every moving van. We use them every day and we sell used ones to anyone who asks.\""), .direct("How did your coffee lid end up in the investigation?", "\"I stopped at a gas station for coffee and threw it away. I didn't know anyone was collecting trash.\""), .direct("What do you think of the DNA match?", "\"I don't understand it. I think the sample is too old and too weak to prove anything.\""), .cross("Your DNA is on a hair on {V}'s blanket. How do you explain that?", "\"I can't. Hair can transfer on a moving blanket, and I handle dozens a week.\""), .cross("Your phone was near all three sites. Isn't that a coincidence?", "\"It's my route. Everyone who works that stretch would show up in the same data.\""), .cross("A fisherman saw a white moving van. You drove one, didn't you?", "\"I drove one for the company. There were several vans, and they were all white.\""), .cross("You've said you didn't know the victims. Did you ever pick up a rider along that highway?", "\"No. I never carried passengers, and I wasn't alone with anyone I didn't know.\""), .cross("You rented a storage unit under another name, didn't you?", "\"I rent a storage unit. I'd rather not discuss why the name on it isn't mine.\"")],
        openings: ("Twelve years ago, three victims were found in a drainage canal, each wrapped in a blue moving blanket. A new task force traced the blankets, a phone, and a discarded coffee lid to {D}.", "The case against {D} is a partial hair sample, a common blanket, and a phone on a route that {D} drives for a living. The defense will show how weak each piece is and what is missing."),
        closings: ("Blankets from a moving company where {D} worked, a phone near all three sites, a fisherman's white van, and DNA on a coffee lid that matches a hair on {V}'s blanket. Together they point to one person.", "A common blanket, a route that hundreds of phones cross, and a hair sample so degraded the State's own lab could only partly read it. The State has not placed {D} with any victim, and a doubtful sample is not proof."),
        timeline: [(0, "{VL}'s body is found wrapped in a blue blanket in a canal."), (6, "The other two bodies are found."), (80, "The investigation stalls."), (4300, "A new task force reviews tower data and the blankets."), (4500, "A coffee lid is collected from {DL}'s trash."), (4560, "The lid DNA matches the hair."), (4565, "{DL} is arrested.")],
        identified: "Blanket records, a tower dump and DNA from a discarded coffee lid.",
        aggravating: ["The offense involved multiple victims", "The offense was especially heinous, atrocious, or cruel"],
        mitigating: ["No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "expertTestimony"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let willForgeryHeirV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.willForgeryHeir",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Son Filed Forged Deed Weeks Before Father's Death", "Notary Journal Shows Notary Was Out of State"],
        law: "forgery",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Forged a deed of {V} with intent to defraud, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, {D} filed a deed at the register of deeds transferring {V}'s farm to {D}. {V} died weeks later. The notary stamp showed a date when the notary was in another state, and a handwriting examiner said the signature was not {V}'s. {DL} says {V} signed it while in the hospital.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Notary Journal", "The notary was out of state on the date stamped."), E(.forensic, 3, "Handwriting Report", "The signature is not {V}'s."), E(.document, 2, "Registry Filing", "{D} filed the deed three weeks before {V}'s death.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Hospital Signing", "{DL} says {V} signed in the hospital.")],
        role: "Register of deeds clerk",
        exam: [.direct("Tell the jury about your job at the register of deeds.", "\"I'm a clerk at the register of deeds. I record deeds, check the notary stamp and seal, and enter the filing in the county's index.\""), .direct("What deed did {D} file?", "\"A deed transferring {V}'s farm to {D}. {DL} brought it to the counter and paid the recording fee.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the notary stamp?", "\"The date on the stamp fell when the notary's own journal shows the notary was in another state. The notary later confirmed that.\""), .direct("What did the handwriting examination show?", "\"A county examiner compared the signature to known samples of {V}'s writing and concluded it was not {V}'s.\""), .direct("When was the deed filed in relation to {V}'s death?", "\"Three weeks before {V} died. The deed was recorded and indexed that day.\""), .direct("What happened after {V} died?", "\"The family challenged the deed, and the county put a hold on the filing.\""), .cross("Do you check signatures at the counter?", "\"No. We check the notary stamp, the legal description, and the recording fee, not the signature.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say anything about how the deed was signed?", "\"{DL} said {V} signed it in the hospital and that {DL} had been asked to file it.\""), .cross("Were you present when {V} signed?", "\"No. I only handle the filing.\""), .cross("Is it unusual for a family member to file a deed for a relative?", "\"No. It happens all the time.\""), .cross("Did the defendant appear nervous or evasive?", "\"No. {D.He} was polite and paid the fee without any questions.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Home health aide",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your job, and how did you know {V}?", "\"I'm a home health aide. I took care of {V} in the hospital during the last three weeks.\""), .direct("Did {V} sign anything that afternoon?", "\"Yes. {V} asked for a pen and a clipboard and signed a paper that {D} had brought.\""), .direct("What condition was {V} in?", "\"Weak but awake. {V} could hold a pen and said the paper was for the farm.\""), .direct("Did you read the paper?", "\"No. It wasn't my business, and I didn't think to read it.\""), .direct("Did {V} say who the paper was for?", "\"Only that it was for {DF}. {V} said {V.he} wanted things taken care of.\""), .direct("Did anyone else witness the signing?", "\"I did, and a nurse looked in. I don't recall anyone else being in the room.\""), .cross("Were you a notary or a witness to the signature?", "\"No. I only saw {V} hold a pen. I couldn't tell the jury the signature was {V}'s.\""), .cross("Was the paper a deed?", "\"I don't know. It was a few pages stapled together.\""), .cross("Did you read {V}'s handwriting before and after that day?", "\"Not closely. I can't say the signature matches.\""), .cross("How long were you in the room?", "\"A few minutes. I was changing a bag and checking vitals.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell you what the paper was before {V} signed it?", "\"No. I didn't hear {DF} explain it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} forged a deed to take {V}'s farm.", "A real signing in a hospital bed."),
