        closings: ("A notary who wasn't there, a signature that isn't {V}'s, and a deed filed three weeks before death. The farm went to the person who filed the deed, and the paperwork does not hold up.", "An aide saw {V} sign something on a clipboard in a hospital bed. A clerk who never checks signatures and a rushed form do not prove forgery, and a farm passing to the one who cared for {V.him} is not a crime."),
